I'll start by thoroughly investigating the profile-related components and their usage across the project before making any changes.Let me investigate the navigation/menu references and the config files more deeply.Let me check the remaining menu components and profile-related components to be thorough.Let me read the full content of the files I'll need to modify that I only have partially (Desktop.vue, VibeDesktop.vue, TabNavigation.vue) and confirm MainMenu.vue.The actual `Desktop.vue` and `VibeDesktop.vue` delegate to `appComponentsMap.js` (the earlier snippets were stale). Let me re-read the remaining files fresh to confirm their current content.Let me do a final exhaustive check for any remaining `'profiles'` tab/route string references and verify component usage.# Analysis & Pre-Thinking

## Core Requirements
Remove the **Profiles** feature UI from the front-end:
1. **Profile view** → `src/views/ProfileView.vue` (list + edit screen)
2. **Profile editor** → `src/components/EditProfile.vue`
3. **All navigation & menu entries** that open it (sidebar rail, top menu, tab bar, mobile menu, quick bar) plus the app registry, route, and route-builder entry.
4. **Keep** `src/components/profiles/ProfileViewer.vue` (explicitly stated as valid — used by `repo/PRFile.vue`).

## Usage / Dependency Investigation (done before deleting)

| Entity | Referenced by | Verdict |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `views/ProfileView.vue` | `config/appComponentsMap.js` (import + `'profiles'` map) **only** | safe to delete + unregister |
| `components/EditProfile.vue` | `views/ProfileView.vue` **only** | safe to delete |
| `config/apps.js → APPS.profiles` | `openProfiles()`, route `profiles`, menus | remove entry |
| `router/index.ts → /:projectName/profiles` | `APPS.profiles.route()` | remove route |
| `router/navigate.js → openProfiles()` | nothing else (unused) | remove method |
| `Menu` (MainMenuItems) / `TabNavigation` / `MobileMenu` / `QuickBar` entries | — | remove entries |
| `components/profiles/ProfileViewer.vue` | `repo/PRFile.vue` | **KEEP** |
| `ProfileCard.vue`, `ProfileAvatar.vue`, `profile/ProfileSelector.vue`, `ChatProfileSelector.vue`, `ProfileDrawer.vue` | Chat sidebar, kanban, selectors | **KEEP** |
| `store/profiles.js`, `$storex.profiles`, `store/project.js` profile actions | still used by chat selectors/mentions | **KEEP** |
| `components/desktop/Desktop.vue`, `VibeDesktop.vue` | consume `appComponentsMap` aggregates (no direct import) | **no change** |
| `components/layout/AppsSection.vue`, `main-menu/MainMenu.vue` | contain **no** Profiles entry | **no change** |

## Doubt → Not deleted (per your "validate if there's any doubt")
- **`src/components/ProfileChatEditor.vue`** — a chat-based *profile editor*. It has **zero importers** (orphan/dead code). It is *not* referenced by `ProfileView.vue`, so it is technically outside "the profile editor". **Left in place** — see Recommendations.
- **`src/components/NavigationBar.vue`** — contains a stray `'profiles'` string in an unused `isSettings` computed. Not a nav/menu entry; left alone.

## Dependencies & Risks
- Removing the `APPS.profiles` entry means any `openApp('profiles')` will log `unknown app` — all such call sites are being removed.
- The route removal drops the deep-link `/profile`; the catch-all redirects unknown paths to `/`.
- No store/data layer is touched, so chat profile selection keeps working.

## Target Files
**Delete (2):** `views/ProfileView.vue`, `components/EditProfile.vue`
**Modify (8):** `config/appComponentsMap.js`, `config/apps.js`, `router/index.ts`, `router/navigate.js`, `components/main-menu/MainMenuItems.vue`, `components/TabNavigation.vue`, `components/MobileMenu.vue`, `components/project/QuickBar.vue`

